  "rationale": "The national split is materially supported. Indonesian satpam is the established term for a security guard, while Malaysian Malay pengawal keselamatan is the standard Malay equivalent. English security guard may occur as code-switching or an imported workplace label in both countries, but it does not displace the distinct ordinary Malay forms. The cue, sense, answers, and relation are aligned. No false-friend contrast is needed because neither answer has a misleading cross-variety meaning.",
  "claim_reviews": [
    {
      "subject": "English cue and sense",
      "conclusion": "“Security guard” and “a person hired to protect a place or property” are accurate and sufficiently specific.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://repositori.kemendikdasmen.go.id/16339/1/Senarai-Istilah-Asing-Indonesia-di-Ruang-Publik.pdf",
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=72508&keyword=security"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "Indonesian answer: satpam",
      "conclusion": "Satpam is an established Indonesian term and directly denotes personnel responsible for security in a specified environment.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://kbbi.web.id/satpam",
        "https://pid.kepri.polri.go.id/satpam/",
        "https://repositori.kemendikdasmen.go.id/16339/1/Senarai-Istilah-Asing-Indonesia-di-Ruang-Publik.pdf"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "Malaysian Malay answer: pengawal keselamatan",
      "conclusion": "Pengawal keselamatan is the standard Malaysian Malay equivalent of “security guard” and is used in official and institutional Malaysian contexts.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=72508&keyword=security",
        "https://www.msig.com.my/BusinessSafeGuardInsuranceProposalForm_F_AD_P66_V1.pdf",
        "https://www.cgso.gov.my/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/Borang-Senarai-Semak-Inspektorat-Pematuhan-Keselamatan-Perlindungan-KPKK-7-Pin.2021.pdf"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "National split and shared equivalents",
      "conclusion": "The split is not materially overstated. English security/security guard can appear in Indonesian and Malaysian workplace or casual usage, but the evidence supports satpam and pengawal keselamatan as the respective established local forms; the shared English usage is a secondary overlap rather than an equal replacement.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://repositori.kemendikdasmen.go.id/16339/1/Senarai-Istilah-Asing-Indonesia-di-Ruang-Publik.pdf",
        "https://mediaindonesia.com/politik-dan-hukum/730227/perbedaan-satpam-dan-security-peran-strategis-dalam-menjaga-keamanan",
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=72508&keyword=security"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "Final relation and false-friend contrast",
      "conclusion": "Different-common-word is appropriate. Satpam and pengawal keselamatan refer to the same general occupation without a misleading false-friend divergence; the empty contrast field is acceptable.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://kbbi.web.id/satpam",
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=72508&keyword=security"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
